          "deckDescription": "One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for three-card Brag where prials (three of a kind), runs, and flushes are the main hands and ace may be high or low in runs.",
          "suitDescription": "Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Flushes (three of the same suit) and running flushes (three consecutive ranks in the same suit) are ranked hands. Suits do not break ties between equal hand types.",
          "rankDescription": "Thirteen ranks per suit; for prials (three of a kind) the three is the highest rank, then two, ace, king down to four. For runs, ace may be high or low (A-2-3 or Q-K-A). Standard Brag order: prial of threes best, then runs, then flushes, then pairs, then high card.",
